// 004.12, 007.6 (T22): Catala-style multi-level exception-to-exception DAG over both
// boolean `Fact`s (replacing `archetypes.eflint`'s self-negating default idiom without
// cyclic negation) and quantitative `Function` definitions, plus unquoted atom compatibility.
Fact legacy-defeasible-atoms Identified by Default, Exception, Overrides, Priority, Over, Rejects, Yields, Conflict.

Fact person Identified by Alice, Bob, Cara.
Fact resident Identified by person.
Fact student Identified by person.
Fact employed Identified by person.

Fact owes-levy Identified by person
  Default r-resident Holds when resident(person)
  Exception r-student Overrides r-resident Rejects when resident(person) && student(person)
  Exception r-working-student Overrides r-student Holds when resident(person) && student(person) && employed(person).

Function tax-rate Identified by person * int
  Default rate-base Yields 20 When resident(person)
  Exception rate-student Overrides rate-base Yields 0 When resident(person) && student(person)
  Exception rate-working Overrides rate-student Yields 10 When resident(person) && student(person) && employed(person).

Scenario catala-exception-to-exception {
  +resident(Alice).
  +resident(Bob).
  +student(Bob).
  +resident(Cara).
  +student(Cara).
  +employed(Cara).

  // Alice: base default applies -> owes-levy, rate 20
  ?owes-levy(Alice).
  ?tax-rate(Alice, 20).
  ?!conflict owes-levy(Alice).

  // Bob: student exception overrides base -> !owes-levy, rate 0
  ?!owes-levy(Bob).
  ?tax-rate(Bob, 0).
  ?!tax-rate(Bob, 20).

  // Cara: working-student exception overrides student exception -> owes-levy, rate 10
  ?owes-levy(Cara).
  ?tax-rate(Cara, 10).
  ?!tax-rate(Cara, 0).
  ?!tax-rate(Cara, 20).
}
